6	     6	 * input always yields the same incidents, ids and order.
7	     7	 *
8	     8	 *   kind                      fact                                                    subject (id input)
9	     9	 *   checker_anomaly           bundle.anomalies[i]                                      anomaly.id
10	    10	 *   probe_contradiction       probe verdict confirmed, winning hypothesis class ≠ honored   probe.id
11	    11	 *   belief_unlearned          beliefEvent → unlearned                                  beliefId|at
12	    12	 *   adversary_downgrade       belief.adversary.verdict ∈ {downgrade, narrow}           beliefId|reviewedAt
13	    13	 *   guard_hold                decision.status = held with missing beliefs              decision.id
14	    14	 *   guard_block               a fired block guard / guard refusal on a decision        decision.id|guardId
15	    15	 *   unsafe_action_prevented   a fired transform guard, or a precheck that stopped a write   decision.id|guardId
16	    16	 *   unsafe_action_executed    grader: decision.grade.unsafe non-empty                  decision.id
17	    17	 *   budget_stop               bundle.status = stopped_budget, or a USD-cap error span  runId / spanId
18	    18	 *   rate_limited              notary.llm span with llm.attempts > 1; tool span with status 429   spanId
19	    19	 *   model_error               notary.llm span with status error                        spanId
20	    20	 *   tool_error                notary.tool.call span with status error or HTTP 5xx      spanId
21	    21	 *
22	    22	 * Resolutions come from the same records: guards compiled/retired, belief status, approvals,
23	    23	 * the retry outcome, the parent span's status. Nothing is inferred beyond what the records show;
24	    24	 * when nothing resolved an incident its resolution is { status: "open", action: "none" }.
25	    25	 */
